course: dictionary
lesson: 12419
title: Words that change: darkening
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Darkening is a word that shows change. It comes from darken, which means to become darker, or to make something darker. The -ing ending shows that the change is happening now.
explain: «The darkening sky told us a storm was coming.» The sky is getting darker, so darkening tells us what is changing. Ask yourself: what is getting darker? The answer is the sky.
explain: Darkening can also describe feelings. «His darkening mood made the whole room go quiet.» Here the mood is becoming angry or sad. Try putting «getting darker» in the sentence in place of darkening. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Darken means to become darker, or to make something darker.
fact: Darkening is the -ing form of darken, and it can also be an adjective, as in a darkening sky.
fact: A darkening mood is a mood that is becoming angry or sad.
fact: In science, darkening shows change: «The banana's skin was darkening as it ripened.»
fact: A good check is to swap in «getting darker» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The darkening clouds rolled over the hills.» What is getting darker? | The hills | *The clouds | The wind | The grass
exercise: «Her face was darkening with anger as she read the note.» What does darkening show? | Her face was being painted | She was laughing | She was going to sleep | *Her feelings were growing angrier
exercise: What is the -ing form of darken? | darkness | *darkening | darkens | darken
test: «The darkening sky warned us to go home.» What does darkening mean here? | Moving very fast | *Getting darker | Making a loud noise | Getting lighter
test: Which word fits? «Her ___ mood showed she was upset.» | sparkling | *darkening | sleeping
exam: «The darkening sky meant night was coming soon.» What does darkening describe? | Rain falling from the clouds | *The sky getting darker | A bird flying home | The sky getting bigger
